# The inittab of the guest's busybox boot, in busybox init's own format,
# id:runlevels:action:command. busybox init takes the id as the terminal it
# opens for the command, its init's console when the id is empty, and
# ignores the runlevels. t3-busybox-init binds this file over the sysvinit
# inittab at /etc/inittab, which busybox would otherwise read: busybox init
# runs every "wait" line of that file, and its lines for runlevels 0 and 6
# halt and restart the guest.
#
# busybox init runs the boot's scripts first, then the boot hook, which
# installs the run's disc as rc.local does under sysvinit, and then starts
# the terminals: vtium on tty2, with init's console as its standard input,
# as sysvinit starts it, and gettys on tty1 and tty3.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::wait:/usr/local/sbin/tier3-install
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty --noclear 38400 tty1
::respawn:/usr/local/sbin/t3-console tty2
tty3::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty3
